Not every norm, not
everything should be normal

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:28.720
and the same way all
the time changes change

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:33.720
and we embrace it, but it
can't be reckless, autocratic

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:37.430
authoritarian, anti-democratic change

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.690
in the United States of
America that people fall into

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.360
because they feel powerless or weak

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:46.770
or frustrated by what is not happening.

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:49.990
We have to fight for that very, very hard.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:52.870
And given what's happening
in these laws being passed

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.430
around the country in
many many legislatures

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:59.290
that are going to make it
harder for people to vote.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.650
I think that is a recipe for a potential

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:05.330
of real implosion of violence.

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:06.830
I mean, because what it's trying to do

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:10.660
is legitimize the steel
actually have a steel

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.231
create the predicate for it.

00:15:13.231 --> 00:15:17.270
And that is gonna require
us to also fight back.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:20.020
So this generation of the Yale students

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:23.960
