00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:04.440
What could Yale be
focusing its attention on

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.300
through our planetary solutions project

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:10.420
that you think is an understudied
aspect of climate change?

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:15.420
Or it's a remediation
that we should seriously

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.793
try to organize that ourselves around.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:20.373
- Direct air capture.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.840
I mean, if we can figure
out how to suck this stuff

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:27.350
